"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[8563],{18563:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"indeksaciya-pensiy-2027-fevral-aprel","locale":"en","title":"Pensions will be indexed twice in 2027: 6.8% in February and 3.3% in April","description":"Insurance pensions will increase by 6.8% from February 1 and 3.3% from April 1 in 2027. How double indexation works and how much it adds.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"Social Fund chairman Sergei Chirkov gave the average old-age insurance pension for nonworking pensioners in 2027 as 30 241 rubles, an increase of 2466 rubles from 2026. Pensions will be indexed in two stages: 6.8% from February 1 and another 3.3% from April 1, a combined 10.3%. Indexation covers more than 37 million insurance-pension recipients, including working pensioners, whose pensions have again been indexed since 2025."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"In 2026, pensions increased once, by 7.6% from January 1. A similar two-stage February and April arrangement existed in law before 2019 and is now returning. The stages serve different purposes. February compensates for the previous year\'s inflation; 6.8% is currently an estimate, with Rosstat calculating the final figure in January. April depends on Social Fund revenue: if wages and related contributions grow faster than prices, the fund has money for an increase above inflation."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"Imagine wages increasing once a year in February by exactly the inflation that has already occurred. Prices rose throughout the previous year while income stayed unchanged, buying less by January. The February increase restores earlier purchasing power but does not repay what was lost during the year. That is how catch-up indexation works. Moving the date to February 1 means pensioners will face new-year prices in January 2027 while still receiving the old pension."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"This explains the difference between the figures. If pensions rise by 10.3%, why does the average increase by only 2466 rubles, about 9%? Because 30 241 rubles is the average pension across the whole of 2027. January still uses the old amount, February and March include one indexation, and only April onward includes both. Our calculation puts the average nonworking pensioner\'s pension from April at about 30.6 thousand rubles, roughly 10% above the 2026 level."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"The real increase depends on inflation. If prices rise by 6.8% in 2026, February\'s indexation only compensates for that, while April\'s 3.3% adds purchasing power above the previous year\'s inflation. Prices will also rise in 2027, consuming part of the increase. Analysts surveyed by the Bank of Russia expect 7.1% inflation for 2026. February indexation follows actual inflation, so it will be larger if prices rise more than estimated. Social pensions are indexed separately from April 1 according to subsistence-minimum growth, provisionally by 6.8%."},{"id":"b006","kind":"paragraph","text":"Working pensioners will also have pensions recalculated from August 1, 2027, for employer contributions paid in 2026, subject to a maximum of 3 pension points. Each person\'s ruble increase differs and depends on the pension amount; the Social Fund personal account will show it. The State Duma still has to adopt the fund\'s draft 2027 budget. The April increase is included in advance on the assumption that wages and contributions will continue growing faster than prices."},{"id":"b007","kind":"heading","text":"How much will pensions be indexed in 2027?"},{"id":"b008","kind":"paragraph","text":"Insurance pensions will rise by 6.8% from February 1, based on estimated 2026 inflation, and by another 3.3% from April 1. Together, the pension rises by 10.3%. Each person\'s ruble increase differs according to the pension amount."},{"id":"b009","kind":"heading","text":"Will working pensioners receive indexation?"},{"id":"b010","kind":"paragraph","text":"Yes. Since 2025, insurance pensions have also been indexed for working pensioners, and both 2027 increases cover them. In addition, pensions will be recalculated from August 1 for employer contributions, up to a maximum of 3 pension points."},{"id":"b011","kind":"heading","text":"Why will the average pension rise by 2466 rubles rather than 10%?"},{"id":"b012","kind":"paragraph","text":"The 30 241 ruble figure is the average across the whole of 2027. January still uses the old pension, February and March include one increase, and only April onward includes both. From April, the average nonworking pensioner\'s pension will be about 30.6 thousand rubles, roughly 10% above 2026."}],"sources":[{"label":"Average old-age insurance pension will increase in 2027","url":"https://www.kommersant.ru/doc/9042520"},{"label":"Insurance pensions will be indexed twice in 2027","url":"https://mintrud.gov.ru/pensions/94"},{"label":"Pensions will be indexed in February and April 2027","url":"https://www.interfax.ru/russia/1119578"},{"label":"Insurance pensions will outpace inflation in 2027","url":"https://aif.ru/society/strahovye-pensii-v-2027-godu-budut-rasti-bystree-inflyacii"},{"label":"Pensions in 2027: double indexation, increase schedule and new amounts","url":"https://news.ru/economics/pensii-v-2027-godu-dvojnaya-indeksaciya-grafik-povyshenij-i-novye-summy"},{"label":"Bank of Russia macroeconomic survey, October 2026","url":"https://www.cbr.ru/content/document/file/193892/survey_pdf.pdf"},{"label":"Pension indexation in 2026","url":"https://www.banki.ru/webview/dialog/articles/40554/"},{"label":"Size of Russia\'s 2027 pension increase disclosed","url":"https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/20/raskryta-summa-uvelicheniya-pensiy-v-rossii-v-2026-godu"},{"label":"Average insurance pension for 2027 announced","url":"https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/21/rossiyanam-nazvali-sredniy-razmer-strahovoy-pensii-v-2027-godu"}],"sourceBodySha256":"dbab3190117599a76dceb4c08cb97459487f6cc30b90ee5c5a928314ad375a22"}')}}]);